415	/**
416	 * The sheet's figures, as the screen shows them: a person's claimed is their counting claims' amounts added up, leaving out corrections;
417	 * their due-total is those claims' figures added up (a claim's figure: its settled due, else the figure a statement
418	 * bound it to, else its amount times the rate in force on its date of the grade in force on its date (the sheet's own, else its parent's, up to three levels up), rounded half up when the claim rounds by a date before the sheet's policy date, else half to even;
419	 * none without a rate) with its late charge added on top while it is overdue, and then — unless it is settled or a correction — at least the sheet's floor in force on its date, n/a when their grade on the sheet's today has no rate then and no counting claim keeps a settled or bound
420	 * figure or one at another grade, and at most the sheet's cap in force on its today (an n/a one is not capped); their overdue-total is the figures (late charge included) of
421	 * those of their claims that are OPEN or PENDING and past their due-by plus their grade's grace on the sheet's today, added up (uncapped). After a change, records one ROLLUP line per person whose figures (overdue-total included) it moved,
422	 * then a TOTALS line when any of the sheet's three totals moved, then — while the sheet's alert threshold is set — an ALERT line, in list order, per person whose due-total went from at or below it (or none) to above it. The sheet's due-total and overdue-total leave out the
423	 * single highest and the single lowest person's figure when three or more people have one (an n/a due-total is none). A claim deferred past the sheet's today counts in none of these. A person's OPEN and PENDING claims dated within one of their holds count in none of these, unless a statement
424	 * binds them; their other claims still do. So too, from the day their retirement date is reached (the sheet's today on or
425	 * after it), do none of a retired person's OPEN and PENDING claims, unless a statement binds them.
426	 */
427	@Service
428	public class Rollup {
